From: AdobeWine
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: Attach and detach threads to the main module built at process start.

A thread started after the program had changed PEB->ImageBaseAddress crashed in loader_init (and on exit in
LdrShutdownThread): both looked the main module up with get_modref( Peb->ImageBaseAddress ), got NULL for an address
that has no modref, and read its TlsIndex. In-process unpackers point ImageBaseAddress at their payload; public #18:
Adobe's Creative_Cloud_Set-Up.exe (32-bit, UPX) on an Intel laptop, c0000005 at loader_init+0x2f4 in 0.4.0's 32-bit
ntdll, right after its first WMI query. Windows keeps its own pointer to the main module's entry and starts the thread.
The modref built at process start is now kept and used for thread attach and detach (the address lookup stays as a
fallback for an ntdll that did not build it).
Test: wine/tests/loader/imagebase.c (32 and 64 bit): crash before, "thread ran" PASS after. Wine's kernel32:loader,
kernel32:thread, ntdll:exception, ntdll:thread on both arches unchanged; regress.sh 17/17.
---
--- a/dlls/ntdll/loader.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/loader.c
@@ -186,6 +186,9 @@
 static RTL_BITMAP tls_expansion_bitmap;
 
 static WINE_MODREF *cached_modref;
+/* the exe as built at process start: threads attach and detach it even after an in-process unpacker pointed
+ * Peb->ImageBaseAddress at its payload, which has no modref (Windows keeps its own pointer too) */
+static WINE_MODREF *main_modref;
 static WINE_MODREF *last_failed_modref;
 
 static LDR_DDAG_NODE *node_ntdll, *node_kernel32;
@@ -3975,7 +3978,7 @@
 
     if (!NtCurrentTeb()->SkipThreadAttach)
     {
-        wm = get_modref( NtCurrentTeb()->Peb->ImageBaseAddress );
+        wm = main_modref ? main_modref : get_modref( NtCurrentTeb()->Peb->ImageBaseAddress );
         mark = &NtCurrentTeb()->Peb->LdrData->InInitializationOrderModuleList;
         for (entry = mark->Blink; entry != mark; entry = entry->Blink)
         {
@@ -4497,7 +4500,7 @@
 
         if (NtCurrentTeb()->WowTebOffset) init_wow64( context );
 
-        wm = build_main_module();
+        wm = main_modref = build_main_module();
         build_ntdll_module();
 #ifdef __arm64ec__
         load_arm64ec_module();
@@ -4545,7 +4548,7 @@
             return;
         }
 
-        wm = get_modref( NtCurrentTeb()->Peb->ImageBaseAddress );
+        wm = main_modref ? main_modref : get_modref( NtCurrentTeb()->Peb->ImageBaseAddress );
     }
 
     NtCurrentTeb()->FlsSlots = fls_alloc_data();
